        "body": "## summary\n\n- distinguish implicit observer attachments from explicit retaining subscriptions while preserving event and server-request delivery\n- allow idle core-created threads with no explicit subscribers to reach the existing 30-minute unload lifecycle\n- use retaining-subscriber semantics for running resume overrides and preserve the full idle grace period across coalesced watcher edges\n\n## why\n\napp-server auto-attaches every initialized connection to internally created threads so clients can observe events and answer requests. those delivery-only attachments currently share subscription bookkeeping with explicit thread/start, thread/resume, and thread/fork requests, so the idle-unload watcher never sees zero subscribers. this leaves otherwise idle threads and their session resources loaded indefinitely\n\n## testing\n\n- just test -p codex-app-server --test-threads=2 (936 passed, 1 skipped)\n- focused implicit/explicit, mixed-state, reactivation, coalesced-edge, and running-resume regressions\n- just fix -p codex-app-server\n- just fmt",
