        "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- replace `codex-protocol`'s direct `reqwest` dependency with `codex-http-client::HttpError` and `http::StatusCode`\n- construct the protocol error fixture through the shared `HttpResponse` alias without importing reqwest\n- remove `codex-protocol` from the temporary reqwest migration exceptions and refresh `Cargo.lock`\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-http-client` is the intended first-party owner of reqwest. Using its existing error alias preserves the concrete error type for downstream consumers while removing transport-specific ownership from the foundational protocol crate.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol` \u2014 267 passed\n- `just test -p codex-api` \u2014 156 passed\n- `cargo deny check bans` \u2014 passed\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check` \u2014 passed\n- `just fmt`",
